p.src:
For one canonical pair, Hamilton’s equations give $V_p=-\frac{\partial H}{\partial q},
  \qquad
  V_q=\frac{\partial H}{\partial p}.$ The divergence is therefore $\begin{aligned}\frac{\partial V_p}{\partial p}
  +\frac{\partial V_q}{\partial q}
  &=
  -\frac{\partial}{\partial p}
    \left(\frac{\partial H}{\partial q}\right)
  +\frac{\partial}{\partial q}
    \left(\frac{\partial H}{\partial p}\right)\\
  &=
  -\frac{\partial^2H}{\partial p\,\partial q}
  +\frac{\partial^2H}{\partial q\,\partial p}
  =0.
  \end{aligned}$

